For any fixed assignment, each component’s vertices can be connected as a tree in \(\prod_i n_i^{n_i-2}\) ways. Since only three extra vertices are distributed, the possible component sizes are obtained by adding 3 to the five initial singleton components. Summing over distributions gives
\[
\sum_{a_1+\cdots+a_5=3}
\frac{3!}{a_1!\cdots a_5!}
\prod_{i=1}^5 (a_i+1)^{a_i-1}
= 280,
\]
where the singleton factor is interpreted as 1. Therefore the answer is **(J) 280**.

